- op: discuss  # ebd8
  at: '2026-08-10T14:38:34Z'  # ebd8
  by: agent  # ebd8
  actor: jgstern_agent  # ebd8
  clock: 3  # ebd8
  nonce: ebd8  # ebd8
  message: "LOCALIZED AND FIXED, 2026-08-10. The item recorded \"Something inside that chain\ndoes not fire. Not localized further.\" It is one condition.\n\nTHE DEFECT. The WI-kuroj return-type-registry lookup in _extract_go_var_types\nguarded on `rhs.type == \"call_expression\"`. `rhs` is `node.children[-1]` of a\n`short_var_declaration`, and that child is an `expression_list` WRAPPER -- never\nthe expression itself. So the condition could not be true for any input, and the\nblock was DEAD CODE from the day it shipped. The registry was built (go.py:4483),\nthreaded through three call layers, and consulted by a branch nothing could reach.\n\nAST evidence:\n    short_var_declaration: left='result'  rightType=expression_list\n                           right child:   type=call_expression text='e.Query()'\n\nWHY THE SIBLING WORKED. `_type_from_rhs` unwrapped the `expression_list` inline\nand therefore resolved `e := &Engine{}` correctly, which is why var_types showed\n{'e': 'Engine', 'result': ''} -- one consumer unwrapping and one not, for the same\nquestion. Both now route through `_unwrap_rhs_expression`.\n\nCONFIRMED BEFORE THE FIX, directly against production's own extractor:\n    registry={'Engine.Query': 'Result'} -> main={'e': 'Engine', 'result': ''}\nand after:\n    registry={'Engine.Query': 'Result'} -> main={'e': 'Engine', 'result': 'Result'}\n\nALL THREE TESTS NOW XPASS, so the xfail(strict=True) marker is removed. strict is\nwhat did the work here: it flipped the suite red the moment the feature started\nworking, which is exactly the signal the marker was placed for. The single unwrap\nfixes all three, including the tuple-return case (`result, _ := e.Query()`).\n\nTHE STALE PRAGMA IS GONE TOO. The item's \"corroborating smell\" was right: the\nblock carried `# pragma: no cover - requires Go tree-sitter grammar` while the\ngrammar is installed. It was excusing itself from coverage on the same false\npremise that kept the tests skipped.\n\nMEASURED ON A REAL REPO, BOTH DIRECTIONS, BOTH DENOMINATORS (alertmanager):\n    call edges          8,322 -> 8,321\n    gained 108, lost 109  -- near 1:1, so these are UPGRADES not inventions\n    external placeholders 1,576 -> 1,467\n    resolution_quality typed_receiver 577 -> 685\nSampled pairs confirm replacement rather than creation:\n    go:external:0-0:isEOF  ->  matcher/parse/token.go:token.isEOF:method\n    go:external:0-0:Next   ->  provider/provider.go:AlertIterator.Next:method\n\n*** 102 OF THE 108 GAINED HAVE A _test.go SOURCE. *** Production-path payoff is\n6, not 108. Quoting 108 alone would overstate it 18x, which is this repo's\nrecurring sizing error and is stated here so the next reader does not repeat it.\n\nPRECISION RISK, DISCLOSED NOT BURIED. The \"typing a receiver re-opens name\ncollisions\" landmine fired exactly once: 107 of 108 gained edges land on a\n`:method` dst, one lands on a `:field` (InhibitRule.hasEqual ->\ntemplate/template.go:Alert.Fingerprint:field). A `calls` edge to a field kind is\nincoherent on its face. It is NOT introduced here -- alertmanager already carries\n266 such edges and this change takes it to 267 -- but those 266 deserve their own\nlook and no item currently covers them."  # ebd8
